  "sport": "floorball",
  "title": "British Bulldogs – get across without losing the ball",
  "description": "All players stand on one side with a ball each. One chaser – the bulldog – stands in the middle. On the signal everyone carries the ball across to the other side, and the bulldog tries to win as many balls as possible. Whoever loses their ball becomes a bulldog too. The more who are caught, the harder it gets to cross.\n\nLevels: 1) The bulldogs have sticks and take the ball. 2) Every attacker also has a tail (a bib tucked into the waistband) that works as an extra life – lose the ball but keep the tail and you get a new ball. 3) The bulldogs have no sticks and only need to take the tail. Fit the area to the number of players. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Look up – find the gap between the bulldogs."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Change direction and speed when a bulldog comes close."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Shield the ball with your body if you are put under pressure."
    }
  ],
  "locale": "en",
